<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Prompts</h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We include the sample prompt templates.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.7.1 </span>Relative Confidence</h4>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para"><pre id="A1.SS7.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
You are an expert in evaluating questions.
Compare the following two questions and
decide which one you are more confident in answering:

Question 1: &lt;Question1&gt;

Question 2: &lt;Question2&gt;

Respond with Question number and reasoning why you are more confident in
answering a given question. Respond with ’&lt;winner&gt;Question 1&lt;/winner&gt;
&lt;reason&gt; your reasoning ...&lt;/reason&gt;’ if you are more confident
that you can answer Question 1 correctly, or &lt;winner&gt;Question 2 &lt;/winner&gt;
&lt;reason&gt; your reasoning ...&lt;/reason&gt;’ if you are more
confident in your ability to answer Question 2 correctly.

Answer:
</pre>
</div>
</section>
